00:00:04.630 --> 00:00:06.869 align:start position:0%
every morning sanumaya bista collects  water from these centuries old stone  taps in dhobigat a suburb of kathmandu  once a week water is also piped into her  home but it's barely enough for her  family's needs  many people come here and wait in line  to collect water it's never empty it's  crowded in the mornings some people come  as early as 3am  across the road women paid to use pond  water to wash clothes  kathmandu's rapidly growing population  is straining the city's already  overwhelmed municipal water system  most people have to buy water from  tankers at high  prices the city relies on aquifers fed  by monsoon rains  but as it expands and demand for water  rises they're running dry  kathmandu is home to 4 million people  the city requires 430 million liters of  water a day less than half that demand  is being supplied residents hope the  ambitious and long delayed melancholy  water supply project to pipe water from  the river to the city will reduce demand  that project is run by the public  utility kukl that's now upgrading  infrastructure to protect water supplies  from the melamchi river  the target of our kukl company is to  distribute the available water  equitably  and without  minimum without more leakages you see as  a network of kathmandu valley is old  more than 100 years so there is a lot of  problem of leakage water leakage that is  why also we are  shifting from old network to new network  which are undergoing now organizations  like smartpani are also seeking  solutions to the city's water shortages  there are very many schools in kathmandu  valley which are struggling to manage  water and provide safe water to their  kids you know so that's why we work with  public schools where there is a dire  need of water and support them with an  alternate resource of water by  harvesting the rain water that is  falling on their own rooftop we're just  filtering it and ensuring that it can be  reused unpredictable monsoon rains and a  rapidly growing city are clearly big  challenges here but many hope that by  conserving water they'll at least start  to reduce them ramyata limbu al-jazeera  kathmandu
 

